  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nTemperatures tick down Friday and Saturday as the upper-level ridge \nsets up over the southeastern CONUS. Highs generally top out in the \nmid-to-upper 90s, with 100 degree temperatures becoming less \nwidespread and more confined to the river valleys. By the latter \nhalf of the weekend and into next week, the ridge begins to shift \nwestward again. As a result, temperatures start to trend back up by \nSunday through at least the middle part of next week. As far as rain \nchances go, upslope flow and a shortwave moving along the western \nperiphery of the ridge will allow scattered showers and storms to \nonce again develop in and around the higher terrain through the \nweekend. Chances range from 10-40% for portions of the Upper Trans-\nPecos, Guadalupe/Delaware Mountains, and Presidio Valley, with \nhigher chances (40-60%) in/near the Davis Mountains and Marfa \nPlateau. Rain chances decrease early next week thanks to increasing \nsubsidence and decreasing moisture as the ridge shifts westward. By \nMonday, only low PoPs (10-30%) are maintained for far western \nportions of the region and in the Davis Mountains, and by Tuesday \nchances drop to about 10% for these same areas.\n\nSprang",
